review.reviewBody:
So I did change it and it was fab.
I had a whole Pineapple I needed to use. So I chopped up some and add it to my pot. Put it on low/med heat. Add half of an chopped onion, About a Tbsp of Molasses , and a Tbsp of coconut Sugar, salt and pepper and powder garlic to taste. I heated it up for about 5 to 8 mins and then took a potato smasher and smashed it:-&gt;
Let it cool for a little while. Added chicken. Let it marinate for 30 mins. Put them on some screwer and then BBQ. After they where on the BBQ for about 4 to 5 mins on each side, then put foil down and placed chicken on foil, dumped left over sauce and allow to cook for 5 to 8 mins in juices. Wait till it boils and the pineapple is cooked. EAT!
